{"crc":"d439b074","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is in the `_escape_args_and_kwargs` method in `sphinx/ext/napoleon/docstring.py`. When an attribute name ends with an underscore (like `hello_`), it's being escaped to `hello\\_`, which shows a visible backslash in the HTML output.\n\nThe fix should only escape trailing underscores for parameter names (where `*args` and `**kwargs` patterns need escaping), not for attribute names. Let me look at how this method is called.\n\nThe `_escape_args_and_kwargs` method is called from `_consume_field`, which handles both parameters and attributes. The escaping of trailing underscores is only needed for parameter names (to prevent RST from interpreting `*args_` or `**kwargs_` patterns), but for attributes like `hello_`, the trailing underscore should not be escaped.\n\nLet me check the current code:\n\n# path: sphinx/ext/napoleon/docstring.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def _escape_args_and_kwargs(self, name: str) -> str:\n        if name.endswith('_'):\n            name = name[:-1] + r'\\_'\n\n        if name[:2] == '**':\n            return r'\\*\\*' + name[2:]\n        elif name[:1] == '*':\n            return r'\\*' + name[1:]\n        else:\n            return name\n=======\n    def _escape_args_and_kwargs(self, name: str) -> str:\n        if name[:2] == '**':\n            return r'\\*\\*' + name[2:]\n        elif name[:1] == '*':\n            return r'\\*' + name[1:]\n        else:\n            return name\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":1},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQY7H56WTX5JF49A3A1Z01A","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQY7H4ZYBWNGVD0MP1C6MT4"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":35,"t":1786436115.586144}
